Orthonym — Third-Party Vendored Artifacts
==========================================

This file records the provenance and licensing of third-party binary
artifacts vendored into this repository and invoked at runtime via
subprocess (no source linkage, no relicensing burden).


centres-cli-1.5.jar
-------------------
- Component:  centres (CIP — Cahn-Ingold-Prelog stereo descriptor labeller)
- Project:    SiMolecule / centres  (reference implementation of the
              Hanson et al. 2018 CIP algorithm; CDK backend)
- Version:    1.5 (built from the `develop` branch @ commit d4b3cf0, pom
              version 1.5-SNAPSHOT; CDK 2.12). Refreshed 2026-06-27 from the
              previously vendored 1.2.1.
- Main-Class: com.simolecule.centres.LabelCip
- Size:       2,421,241 bytes (vendored UNMODIFIED; shaded fat-jar produced by
              `mvn -pl cdk -am package -DskipTests`).
- License:    BSD-2-Clause (per the upstream LICENSE file and every source
              header; Copyright (c) 2020, John Mayfield). NOTE: the upstream
              Maven pom <licenses> block inconsistently lists LGPL-3.0, but the
              authoritative LICENSE file + source headers are BSD-2-Clause.
- Usage:      Invoked out-of-process as an unmodified standalone jar via a
              subprocess (`java -jar centres-cli-1.5.jar -i smi <file>`)
              by src/orthonym/perception/centres_bridge.py. Orthonym does
              NOT link against, statically embed, or modify the jar.
              `centres_bridge._find_centres_jar()` globs `centres-cli-*.jar`
              and selects the highest version, so a future engine update needs
              only a new jar dropped in (no code change).
- Optional:   Adoption is env-gated (ORTHONYM_USE_CENTRES_CIP, default ON).
              When the jar or a Java runtime is absent, Orthonym falls back to
              RDKit's rdCIPLabeler and never hard-fails a name on a missing JVM.
- Suite:      centres 1.5 scores 279/290 on the Hanson 2018 CIP Validation
              Suite (vs 281 on 1.2.1 and 235 for RDKit's rdCIPLabeler). The −2
              vs 1.2.1 is two exotic cyclic-cumulene axial (M/P) labels (VS078,
              VS287); all R/S/E/Z labels are byte-identical to 1.2.1, and
              Orthonym computes allene/axial CIP independently, so naming is
              unaffected. See tests/integration/test_cip_validation.py.
- Source:     https://github.com/SiMolecule/centres


